WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.368 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Our next guest
is a talented actress

00:00:01.368 --> 00:00:03.370 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know from films
such as "Wind River,"

00:00:03.370 --> 00:00:04.070 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
"Ingrid Goes West,"

00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:06.339 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the Avengers
and Captain America franchises

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:09.909
She returns as Wanda Maximof
in Marvel's "WandaVision,"

00:00:09.909 --> 00:00:12.312 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is currently streaming
on Disney+.

00:00:12.312 --> 00:00:14.414 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Let's take a look.

00:00:15.081 --> 00:00:17.017 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Loud banging ]
-[ Gasps ]

00:00:17.017 --> 00:00:18.051 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
What was that?

00:00:18.051 --> 00:00:20.820 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
[ Music trills ]

00:00:22.188 --> 00:00:24.858 size:78% position:39% line:92%
[ Banging continues ]

00:00:27.427 --> 00:00:29.129 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Wanda?
-Yes, dear.

00:00:29.129 --> 00:00:32.699 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Are you using your powers
to turn on the light?

00:00:32.699 --> 00:00:34.067 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes, dear.

00:00:34.067 --> 00:00:36.536 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-Allow me, sweetheart.

00:00:37.737 --> 00:00:40.407 size:78% position:39% line:92%
[ Crickets chirping ]

00:00:41.341 --> 00:00:43.109 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-What do you see?

00:00:43.109 --> 00:00:45.879 line:92%
-Only your lovely rose bushes.

00:00:45.879 --> 00:00:46.546 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-That's all?

00:00:46.546 --> 00:00:48.648 align:start size:94% position:6%
Are you using your
night vision, Vision?

00:00:48.648 --> 00:00:51.117 size:84% position:42%
-I assure you, my love,
I see nothing amiss.

00:00:51.117 --> 00:00:53.119 align:start size:94% position:6%
You have absolutely
no reason to be --

00:00:53.119 --> 00:00:54.988 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Banging ]
Aah!

00:00:54.988 --> 00:00:57.157 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:58.958 --> 00:00:59.793 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-You were saying?

00:00:59.793 --> 00:01:03.129
-Please welcome back to
the show Elizabeth Olsen.

00:01:03.129 --> 00:01:04.431 size:88% position:44% line:92%
Hi, Lizzie! How are you?

00:01:04.431 --> 00:01:07.167 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-Hi! I'm -- I'm good.

00:01:07.167 --> 00:01:08.401 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
How are you doing?

00:01:08.401 --> 00:01:09.135 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I'm doing well.

00:01:09.135 --> 00:01:10.303 line:92%
You're joining us from London.

00:01:10.303 --> 00:01:11.704 align:start size:94% position:6%
Hopefully it's not
too late there.

00:01:11.704 --> 00:01:14.374 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, I know how late it is.
I understand time zones.

00:01:14.374 --> 00:01:17.510 align:start size:94% position:6%
But hopefully it's not
past your bedtime.

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:18.845 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Um, no. It's fine.

00:01:18.845 --> 00:01:23.650 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, I'm, like, properl
caffeinated, I think,

00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:27.454 size:78% position:39%
and have the shakes,
so I think I'm ready.

00:01:27.454 --> 00:01:27.987 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:27.987 --> 00:01:31.191 align:start size:94% position:6%
Now, I think a lot of people
living in the States

00:01:31.191 --> 00:01:33.693 align:start size:94% position:6%
long for travel
and the idea of escaping

00:01:33.693 --> 00:01:37.163 align:start size:94% position:6%
this sort of COVID existence
we're living here.

00:01:37.163 --> 00:01:41.201 align:start size:94% position:6%
But London, sadly,
is no party either.

00:01:41.201 --> 00:01:41.901 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-No.

00:01:41.901 --> 00:01:43.970 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was really excited
to come to London

00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:48.808 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause it sounded far more ope
than L.A. and New York wer

00:01:48.808 --> 00:01:50.877 line:92%
most of the year last year

00:01:50.877 --> 00:01:54.380 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I got here the day befor
they announced

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:55.448 size:81% position:41% line:92%
their second lockdown.

00:01:55.448 --> 00:01:58.151 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then the world opened up
for three weeks here,

00:01:58.151 --> 00:02:00.587 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we have been living
in a lockdown

00:02:00.587 --> 00:02:04.124 size:88% position:44%
since like mid-December,
and will be till March.

00:02:04.124 --> 00:02:07.427 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, it is
outstanding wallpaper.

00:02:07.427 --> 00:02:08.828 align:start size:94% position:6%
I will say that.
-Thank you.

00:02:08.828 --> 00:02:10.797 align:start size:94% position:6%
I feel like my skin
is blending into it.

00:02:10.797 --> 00:02:13.633 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, I'm kind of worried
about this, like, weird ligh

00:02:13.633 --> 00:02:14.934 size:88% position:44% line:92%
that's on my face and...

00:02:14.934 --> 00:02:16.002 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know.
-No. You look great.

00:02:16.002 --> 00:02:17.470 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's a perfect match.
-Right.

00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:20.707
-It's so nice when actor
and wallpaper can coexist

00:02:20.707 --> 00:02:22.142 line:92%
the way you are right now.

00:02:22.142 --> 00:02:23.776 line:92%
-Great. That was my goal.

00:02:23.776 --> 00:02:24.444 size:75% position:38% line:92%
It's a treasure map.

00:02:24.444 --> 00:02:26.946 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm in a children's room
in my rental.

00:02:26.946 --> 00:02:28.481 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:28.481 --> 00:02:31.384 line:92%
So, this show is so very good.

00:02:31.384 --> 00:02:35.021 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm glad that we're talkin
after four episodes

00:02:35.021 --> 00:02:37.290 align:start size:94% position:6%
because whenever you talk
to anyone

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:39.292 line:92%
in a Marvel project like this,

00:02:39.292 --> 00:02:40.560 line:92%
you cannot talk ahead at all

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:41.828 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I feel like
after four episodes,

00:02:41.828 --> 00:02:46.966 align:start size:94% position:6%
we at least have a better sens
of what this show is about

00:02:46.966 --> 00:02:49.903 align:start size:94% position:6%
Has it been hard
doing press about...

00:02:49.903 --> 00:02:51.771 align:start size:94% position:6%
I feel like
of the Marvel projects,

00:02:51.771 --> 00:02:53.339 line:92%
this one maybe has more secrec

00:02:53.339 --> 00:02:57.110 align:start size:94% position:6%
and more twists behind it
as any.

00:02:57.110 --> 00:02:59.312 line:92%
-Yeah. It's really complicated

00:02:59.312 --> 00:03:03.016 align:start size:94% position:6%
I want to talk about
all the sitcoms.

00:03:03.016 --> 00:03:07.253 size:84% position:42%
I want to talk about
how it's like a sitcom,

00:03:07.253 --> 00:03:08.421 size:81% position:41% line:92%
but not just a sitcom.

00:03:08.421 --> 00:03:11.191
And how do you tease that
and keep people interested

00:03:11.191 --> 00:03:14.794 align:start size:94% position:6%
who want the action and then
get new people interested

00:03:14.794 --> 00:03:15.562 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
in the sitcom part,

00:03:15.562 --> 00:03:18.498 align:start size:94% position:6%
and hopefully you don't lose
them in the action.

00:03:18.498 --> 00:03:20.733 line:92%
So, yeah, but it's always fun.

00:03:20.733 --> 00:03:22.969 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, it's fun to see
fan reactions.

00:03:22.969 --> 00:03:25.572 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think that's what
I look forward to most.

00:03:25.572 --> 00:03:28.007 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean this
with all sincerity --

00:03:28.007 --> 00:03:29.442 align:start size:94% position:6%
One of the joys
of watching this show

00:03:29.442 --> 00:03:33.646 align:start size:94% position:6%
is realizing that you
would have been a great acto

00:03:33.646 --> 00:03:36.349 align:start size:94% position:6%
in literally every
generation of sitcoms.

00:03:36.349 --> 00:03:40.386 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Both laugh ]
Because you are so good

00:03:40.386 --> 00:03:40.954 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
and authentic

00:03:40.954 --> 00:03:44.757 align:start size:94% position:6%
in these styles from the '50
and '60s and '70s.

00:03:44.757 --> 00:03:48.761
That must have been one of the
most fun parts of doing this

00:03:48.761 --> 00:03:50.129 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-It was. It was so --

00:03:50.129 --> 00:03:53.166 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, I feel like
any actor has...

00:03:53.166 --> 00:03:56.769 align:start size:94% position:6%
It feels like a gift when yo
get to do a period piece

00:03:56.769 --> 00:03:57.670 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
or a genre piece.

00:03:57.670 --> 00:04:00.573 size:78% position:39%
And we got to do that
every single episode

00:04:00.573 --> 00:04:01.541 size:88% position:44% line:92%
and change what that was

00:04:01.541 --> 00:04:04.711 size:78% position:39%
and try and replicate
even, like, the lens,

00:04:04.711 --> 00:04:07.113 line:92%
the lighting, mannerisms.

00:04:07.113 --> 00:04:08.448 line:92%
The whole thing was just..

00:04:08.448 --> 00:04:09.649 line:92%
And then also getting to, like

00:04:09.649 --> 00:04:13.186 align:start size:94% position:6%
nod to so many
beautiful sitcoms.

00:04:13.186 --> 00:04:15.455 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then I had Kathryn Hah
by my side,

00:04:15.455 --> 00:04:18.458 size:78% position:39%
who is just the queen
of all things comedy.

00:04:18.458 --> 00:04:20.493 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so, it was...
And then, obviously,

00:04:20.493 --> 00:04:22.161 align:start size:94% position:6%
Paul Bettany
did such a great job

00:04:22.161 --> 00:04:26.366
with all the physical comedy
and it was very Dick Van Dyke.

00:04:26.366 --> 00:04:28.134 size:84% position:42% line:92%
And it's been such a...

00:04:28.134 --> 00:04:30.503 size:88% position:44%
It was a really big joy,
and really, really hard,

00:04:30.503 --> 00:04:32.505 size:88% position:44% line:92%
but it was a lot of fun.

00:04:32.505 --> 00:04:33.840 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-You filmed the first --

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:35.408 align:start size:94% position:6%
This was, of course,
before COVID.

00:04:35.408 --> 00:04:37.944 align:start size:94% position:6%
But you filmed the first
episode, I believe,

00:04:37.944 --> 00:04:40.179 align:start size:94% position:6%
in front of a live
studio audience.

00:04:40.179 --> 00:04:42.015 line:92%
Was that -- I mean, I imagin

00:04:42.015 --> 00:04:44.951 align:start size:94% position:6%
that's not something
that you had done before.

00:04:44.951 --> 00:04:46.185 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
How was that?

00:04:46.185 --> 00:04:48.655 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I've only done, you know,
theater before,

00:04:48.655 --> 00:04:51.190 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then, like,
going on your show

00:04:51.190 --> 00:04:52.925 line:92%
or, like, other shows like it.

00:04:52.925 --> 00:04:58.698
And I get way more nervous
for these kinds of things

00:04:58.698 --> 00:04:59.732 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
than anything else.

00:04:59.732 --> 00:05:03.703
I feel like I was really nervous
before with the sitcom

00:05:03.703 --> 00:05:06.506 align:start size:94% position:6%
because it was our first tim
filming this show

00:05:06.506 --> 00:05:07.974 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it was in front
of an audience.

00:05:07.974 --> 00:05:11.377 size:75% position:38%
So we're just, like,
filming our failure.

00:05:11.377 --> 00:05:12.378 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know,
if it were going to fail,

00:05:12.378 --> 00:05:14.380 align:start size:94% position:6%
it was gonna fail in front o
a bunch of people.

00:05:14.380 --> 00:05:16.883 align:start size:94% position:6%
But then I get into a rhythm
'cause I know how to --

00:05:16.883 --> 00:05:18.117 align:start size:94% position:6%
I feel like I know
how to do my job.

00:05:18.117 --> 00:05:20.386 align:start size:94% position:6%
But this I don't know
how to do ever,

00:05:20.386 --> 00:05:23.089 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, like, I have to do
breathing exercises

00:05:23.089 --> 00:05:25.758 size:75% position:38%
before, like, seeing
your friendly face.

00:05:25.758 --> 00:05:26.426 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Both laugh ]

00:05:26.426 --> 00:05:29.329 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Do you -- So, are you
enjoying this era

00:05:29.329 --> 00:05:31.497 align:start size:94% position:6%
of getting to do
sort of this press junket

00:05:31.497 --> 00:05:34.167 align:start size:94% position:6%
without having to come
to an actual studio

00:05:34.167 --> 00:05:36.636 size:75% position:38%
where you have to do
breathing exercises?

00:05:36.636 --> 00:05:37.937 line:92%
-Yeah. You know, I don't know.

00:05:37.937 --> 00:05:40.540 align:start size:94% position:6%
I feel like the trap door
usually freaks me out

00:05:40.540 --> 00:05:44.010 align:start size:94% position:6%
before entering the stage
on night shows.

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:46.713 line:92%
But I like seeing you in person,

00:05:46.713 --> 00:05:48.381 line:92%
and so it's a bit strange,

00:05:48.381 --> 00:05:49.615 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I really don't miss
a junket.

00:05:49.615 --> 00:05:55.788
You know, the four-minute cycl
for 12 hours of strangers is -

00:05:55.788 --> 00:05:57.757 line:92%
and some familiar faces, but..

00:05:57.757 --> 00:05:59.492 size:84% position:42% line:92%
That's nicer from home.

00:05:59.492 --> 00:06:02.662 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You sort of mentioned
that this is a show

00:06:02.662 --> 00:06:04.297 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, you know,
obviously, a universe

00:06:04.297 --> 00:06:08.735
where there is a great amoun
of fan interaction with it

00:06:08.735 --> 00:06:11.070 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I feel as though
with Easter eggs

00:06:11.070 --> 00:06:14.273
and with characters from
different parts of this universe

00:06:14.273 --> 00:06:15.441 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
showing up,

00:06:15.441 --> 00:06:17.510
is that ever something
that you did with a show?

00:06:17.510 --> 00:06:19.879
Where, you know, it would ai
and then you would sort of g

00:06:19.879 --> 00:06:24.684
and read about it in that
sort of recappy fan service way?

00:06:24.684 --> 00:06:28.488 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No. I'm, like, anti, like
looking at everything

00:06:28.488 --> 00:06:30.223 align:start size:94% position:6%
on the internet,
generally speaking,

00:06:30.223 --> 00:06:32.191 align:start size:94% position:6%
when it comes to something
I'm passionate about

00:06:32.191 --> 00:06:34.560 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause I don't want
anyone else's ideas.

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:35.795 size:81% position:41% line:92%
I don't want spoilers.

00:06:35.795 --> 00:06:38.164 align:start size:94% position:6%
I usually binge
"Game of Thrones"

00:06:38.164 --> 00:06:40.066 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
after it's on air,

00:06:40.066 --> 00:06:44.670 align:start size:94% position:6%
so I'm really good
at avoiding stuff.

00:06:44.670 --> 00:06:45.905 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And, yeah, so, no.

00:06:45.905 --> 00:06:47.807 align:start size:94% position:6%
I also never cared about,
like, anything

00:06:47.807 --> 00:06:50.743 size:75% position:38%
that much as a child
to, like, seek out,

00:06:50.743 --> 00:06:52.812 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know,
forums or something.

00:06:52.812 --> 00:06:56.082
-The weird thing, and I thin
it really speaks to the fact

00:06:56.082 --> 00:06:57.216 size:88% position:44% line:92%
that I was probably a --

00:06:57.216 --> 00:07:00.153 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was a child a lot longer ago
than you, but...

00:07:00.153 --> 00:07:01.654 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, I feel like I would've -
-[ Laughing ]

00:07:01.654 --> 00:07:02.789 align:start size:94% position:6%
See, I also don't think
they had those.

00:07:02.789 --> 00:07:05.258
-Yeah, right. I was like, "Oh,
yeah, why didn't I do that?"

00:07:05.258 --> 00:07:08.728
Oh, right, 'cause it was, like
in the back of a comic book.

00:07:08.728 --> 00:07:10.863 align:start size:94% position:6%
It wasn't like you
could go online.

00:07:10.863 --> 00:07:12.799 line:92%
You had to do a lot more work.

00:07:12.799 --> 00:07:13.666 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Was there a...

00:07:13.666 --> 00:07:15.968 size:88% position:44%
You know, you mentioned
that, like, those shows,

00:07:15.968 --> 00:07:19.772
those old sitcoms, which, again,
like, you know, I wasn't -

00:07:19.772 --> 00:07:21.107 line:92%
I fortunately wasn't aroun

00:07:21.107 --> 00:07:23.643 align:start size:94% position:6%
when those shows were airing
in the '50s and '60s.

00:07:23.643 --> 00:07:26.646 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I feel like when I was
home sick from school,

00:07:26.646 --> 00:07:27.914 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I would watch them.

00:07:27.914 --> 00:07:29.215 line:92%
And I kind of underestimated

00:07:29.215 --> 00:07:31.184 size:78% position:39%
exactly how beautiful
and fun they were.

00:07:31.184 --> 00:07:34.887
And I think that's one of th
sweetest things about this sho

00:07:34.887 --> 00:07:39.325
is it is really an homage
to the way storytelling was done

00:07:39.325 --> 00:07:41.527 line:92%
in a sitcom form that far back

00:07:41.527 --> 00:07:44.831 align:start size:94% position:6%
Did you feel, like,
how warm it was to do?

00:07:44.831 --> 00:07:47.834 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
And also, I mean, it was..

00:07:47.834 --> 00:07:50.303 align:start size:94% position:6%
The family sitcom
throughout the eras,

00:07:50.303 --> 00:07:52.138 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, even just like
"Three's Company,"

00:07:52.138 --> 00:07:53.773 align:start size:94% position:6%
which isn't really
a family sitcom,

00:07:53.773 --> 00:07:55.541 line:92%
but the amount of joy you ge

00:07:55.541 --> 00:07:58.544 align:start size:94% position:6%
from watching people
have a good time,

00:07:58.544 --> 00:08:01.113 line:92%
it's such -- it's such a fun..

00:08:01.113 --> 00:08:03.182 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, I guess it's like
a form of empathy.

00:08:03.182 --> 00:08:06.519 align:start size:94% position:6%
You have to enjoy
someone else's enjoyment.

00:08:06.519 --> 00:08:09.555 size:88% position:44% line:92%
But it really felt good.

00:08:09.555 --> 00:08:13.626 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then the switch to other
elements of this show

00:08:13.626 --> 00:08:17.663
felt so strange
because it felt so good to be --

00:08:17.663 --> 00:08:21.100 align:start size:94% position:6%
to be a fool and to try
and make one another laugh

00:08:21.100 --> 00:08:23.202 align:start size:94% position:6%
And also our director,
Matt Shakman,

00:08:23.202 --> 00:08:28.441 align:start size:94% position:6%
just, like, oozes warmth
and friendliness and kindness.

00:08:28.441 --> 00:08:31.377 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he had like three
different viruses

00:08:31.377 --> 00:08:33.579 align:start size:94% position:6%
directing all these episodes
[ Laughs ]

00:08:33.579 --> 00:08:36.749 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm convinced he had COVID
in December.

00:08:36.749 --> 00:08:37.850 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
He got so sick.

00:08:37.850 --> 00:08:40.920 size:81% position:41%
And he was -- he was
really like our leader

00:08:40.920 --> 00:08:44.257 align:start size:94% position:6%
throughout all this
and directed the whole thing

00:08:44.257 --> 00:08:45.958 align:start size:94% position:6%
with just so much warmth,
genuinely.

00:08:45.958 --> 00:08:48.995 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's really great. I also -
I went out of my way

00:08:48.995 --> 00:08:52.331 align:start size:94% position:6%
